(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[26 1 "// _ssl's SSL objects (queue 209): _SSLSocket over a socket or two MemoryBIOs, SSLSession and MemoryBIO."] [27 1 "//"] [28 1 "// The pipe adapter. Go's tls.Conn wants a net.Conn it may block on; OpenSSL's callers (ssl.py over a"] [29 1 "// non-blocking socket, asyncio's SSLProtocol over MemoryBIOs) want SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ and an operation"] [30 1 "// resumed by the next call. So each SSL object runs its tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own (the engine) over"] [31 1 "// an in-memory transport: the engine's Read takes what the Python side fed it and, when there is nothing,"] [32 1 "// tells the Python side it wants input and waits; its Write appends to the bytes to send. Control alternates"] [33 1 "// strictly (the Python thread waits on the engine's event with the GIL released, the engine waits on the"] [34 1 "// Python side's resume), so the engine touches no Python object and the transport's buffers have one owner at"] [35 1 "// a time. The Python side feeds the engine one TLS record at a time (its header, then its length), never"] [36 1 "// more, so after an unwrap the plain bytes behind close_notify stay in the socket as with OpenSSL. A callback"] [37 1 "// the engine needs (the SNI callback) runs on the Python thread with the GIL. Writes and close_notify, which"] [38 1 "// never wait for input, are made on the Python thread directly once the handshake is done (tls.Conn's write"] [39 1 "// side is independent of its read side)."] [62 1 "// sslEngine is the goroutine side: the tls.Conn and its transport's buffers."] [74 2 "// alert is the description OpenSSL would send, 0 when none: the SNI callback's (its *al; Go's server sends"] [75 2 "// internal_error when GetConfigForClient fails), a failed verification's (ssl_x509err2alert; Go sends"] [76 2 "// bad_certificate). The transport puts it in Go's alert record while that is in the clear: always for the"] [77 2 "// SNI callback (before the server's hello), under TLS 1.2 for a verification."] [104 98 "// a fatal alert in the clear"] [119 1 "// call runs f on the Python thread (from the engine)."] [140 1 "// pySSLSocket is an SSL object (PySSLSocket)."] [144 24 "// nil: over MemoryBIOs"] [164 24 "// the incoming record being fed, for the message callback"] [165 24 "// the bytes at the head of the engine's output already traced (a socket's unsent rest)"] [166 24 "// the version the message callback reports: the server hello's, once seen"] [176 1 "// sslVerifyError is a certificate verification failure: OpenSSL's code and message."] [184 1 "// ---- the session cache of one connection: the session given, the session received ----"] [199 2 "// the session's id: its state's digest, so a resumed session renewed by the server keeps it (OpenSSL keeps"] [200 2 "// the session id across a resumption)"] [217 1 "// ---- the configuration ----"] [261 1 "// autoChain is OpenSSL's automatic chain (ssl_add_cert_chain without SSL_MODE_NO_AUTO_CHAIN): a certificate"] [262 1 "// loaded without its chain is sent with the chain the context's store builds for it, as far as it goes (the"] [263 1 "// partial chain of a failed X509_verify_cert too), its root included."] [297 1 "// serverConfig is GetConfigForClient: the SNI callback run on the Python thread (it may switch the socket's"] [298 1 "// context), the configuration made of the context then in force, ALPN without a protocol in common answered"] [299 1 "// with none (CPython's callback returns SSL_TLSEXT_ERR_NOACK; Go's server would refuse the handshake)."] [311 19 "// replaced since the handshake looked"] [316 5 "// _servername_callback: PyErr_FormatUnraisable, then SSL_AD_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE"] [322 5 "// an integer is the alert's description; anything else SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR, with the unraisable"] [339 3 "// OP_NO_TICKET stops TLS 1.2's tickets only: OpenSSL's TLS 1.3 server then sends stateful tickets, which a"] [340 3 "// client sees as tickets. Go's switch covers both versions, so it follows the version this hello gets."] [379 1 "// verify is _ssl's verification (OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert with the context's store, then X509_check_host when"] [380 1 "// check_hostname): the codes of OpenSSL's x509_vfy.h."] [397 3 "// the alert OpenSSL sends for the code (ssl_x509err2alert): Go sends bad_certificate, which the transport"] [398 3 "// rewrites while the alert is in the clear (TLS 1.2; TLS 1.3's is under the handshake keys)"] [409 62 "// a fallback root's constraint"] [413 5 "// Go refuses SHA-1 (and MD5) signatures; OpenSSL refuses them from security level 1 on (63 bits)"] [449 2 "// the security level's checks of X509_verify_cert (check_key_level, check_auth_level): the leaf's key, then"] [450 2 "// each issuer's key and each signature but the trust anchor's"] [465 30 "// VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF (and _CHAIN, which checks the leaf too)"] [489 31 "// VERIFY_X509_STRICT: RFC 5280's AKI on a certificate not self-issued"] [508 1 "// sslCheckHost is X509_check_host / X509_check_ip_asc: 0 when the certificate names host, else 62 (or 64 for an"] [509 1 "// address). The subject's common name is looked at only without a DNS name and without"] [510 1 "// HOSTFLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT; a wildcard only as the whole leftmost label, over one label, with at least two"] [511 1 "// labels after it."] [547 1 "// sslVerifyAlert is ssl_x509err2alert: the alert for a verification code (certificate_unknown when not listed)."] [551 13 "// unknown_ca"] [553 13 "// bad_certificate"] [555 13 "// certificate_expired"] [557 13 "// certificate_revoked"] [559 13 "// decrypt_error"] [561 13 "// unsupported_certificate"] [563 13 "// internal_error"] [565 12 "// certificate_unknown"] [568 1 "// ---- errors ----"] [570 1 "// sslReasons are OpenSSL's reasons of the alerts a peer sends, by alert number."] [584 1 "// sslGoReasons are OpenSSL's reasons for Go's own handshake errors, by the start of their text."] [599 1 "// sslReasonText is ERR_reason_error_string's form of a reason: lower case, words apart."] [617 1 "// raiseErr is PySSL_SetError for an operation's Go error: the exception CPython's _ssl raises for what OpenSSL"] [618 1 "// would have reported."] [661 1 "// ---- the transport's two ends on the Python side ----"] [678 1 "// need is how much the record being fed still needs: its header's rest, then its body's."] [688 74 "// from a record's start"] [697 16 "// not a TLS record: the engine refuses its header"] [713 1 "// ---- the message callback (_PySSL_msg_callback) ----"] [714 1 "//"] [715 1 "// OpenSSL calls it from its record layer with each record's header and each message in the clear. The port sees"] [716 1 "// the records on the wire, where the transport carries them: each record's header (SSL3_RT_HEADER), and the"] [717 1 "// messages of the records still in the clear (the handshake's messages up to the change of keys, change cipher"] [718 1 "// spec, alerts). A record sent or received under the keys is seen by its header alone: Go's tls.Conn keeps its"] [719 1 "// keys, so TLS 1.2's Finished and TLS 1.3's encrypted handshake (and SSL3_RT_INNER_CONTENT_TYPE) are not reported."] [721 1 "// sslMsgTrace is one direction's state: whether its records are under the keys, a handshake message's bytes so far."] [729 1 "// traceIn reports the incoming record just fed (flush reports the outgoing ones)."] [750 26 "// before the server hello: the highest version the context allows, as OpenSSL's"] [755 21 "// change cipher spec is in the clear (TLS 1.3's too, middlebox compatibility's)"] [756 4 "// SSL3_MT_CHANGE_CIPHER_SPEC; OpenSSL 3.5 reports a received one under TLS 1.3 only (TLS 1.2's"] [757 4 "// record layer consumes it unreported)"] [781 22 "// the server hello names the version"] [788 49 "// the rest of the handshake is under the keys"] [797 1 "// sslHelloVersion is a server hello's version: its supported_versions extension's, else its legacy version."] [849 1 "// takeCbErr is PySSL_ChainExceptions after an operation that succeeded: a callback's exception is raised."] [856 1 "// fill feeds the engine the next bytes of the current record: false when they are not there yet (a"] [857 1 "// non-blocking socket, an empty incoming BIO)."] [915 1 "// flush sends what the engine wrote: into the outgoing BIO, or to the socket (a non-blocking one's rest kept,"] [916 1 "// SSLWantWriteError)."] [978 1 "// step hands control to the engine, starting op (nil: resuming it), until it waits for input or is done; the"] [979 1 "// callbacks it asks for run here."] [1000 1 "// drive runs an engine operation (resuming the one in flight first) to its end: OpenSSL's loop of SSL_do_handshake"] [1001 1 "// or SSL_read with the socket's waits; SSLWantReadError when its input is not there yet."] [1066 1 "// ---- the methods ----"] [1080 2 "// close_notify received: SSL_read's zero return is 0 bytes while it is the only shutdown seen"] [1081 2 "// (SSL_RECEIVED_SHUTDOWN), SSLZeroReturnError once this side sent its own"] [1188 27 "// the peer closed the transport: SSL_shutdown's second call gives up"] [1203 1 "// ---- wrap ----"] [1318 1 "// ---- SSLSession ----"] [1329 1 "// ---- MemoryBIO ----"] [1496 21 "// SSL_get_client_ciphers is a server's"] [1583 4 "// a resumed session keeps its id and time (a ticket the server renewed only replaces its state)"] [1595 5 "// OpenSSL's session of a connection that got no ticket (yet): a TLS 1.2 session id (none on a"] [1596 5 "// server that sends a ticket); a TLS 1.3 client's has no id before its first ticket"] [1612 2 "// SSLSession"] [1626 23 "// an OpenSSL server's hint, as CPython's references see it"] [1639 2 "// MemoryBIO"] [1689 1 "// ---- PKCS #8 encryption (PBES2 with PBKDF2, RFC 8018), which Go's x509 does not read ----"] [1787 1 "// sslTimeout is the TimeoutError of an operation past the socket's timeout (the handshake's message with"] [1788 1 "// ERRSTR's prefix, as _ssl.c has it)."] [1796 1 "// sslPBKDF2 is RFC 8018's PBKDF2 with HMAC over prf (crypto/pbkdf2's Key is generic, which goi's table does not"] [1797 1 "// call)."] [1823 1 "// sslDistrustedSPKI are the SHA-256 digests of the public keys _ssl refuses in any chain (Modules/_ssl/"] [1824 1 "// distrusted_spki.h, gh-160040: the compromised eMudhra intermediates)."] [1847 1 "// afterHandshake is what OpenSSL keeps of a finished handshake: the context's session statistics, and the"] [1848 1 "// anchor its by-hash lookup loaded from a capath directory, now in the store (get_ca_certs lists it)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[91 25] [104 19] [203 39] [204 26] [211 24] [246 38] [251 33] [271 57] [276 16] [276 79] [324 29] [366 22] [451 28] [496 38] [497 63] [513 28] [641 29] [672 19] [782 34] [811 34] [1005 42] [1058 43] [1116 25] [1124 57] [1132 28] [1136 19] [1139 32] [1142 56] [1148 25] [1155 27] [1162 19] [1170 34] [1194 59] [1247 44] [1263 31] [1293 31] [1362 28] [1368 33] [1429 33] [1657 33] [1802 16] [1802 35] [1808 13] [1808 23] [1812 14] [1812 21] [1821 54] [1863 25]] :go/trails [[581 127] [596 76] [1833 68]]} (go/file "builtins_ssl_conn.go" :imports [


